// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/petal_issues_viz.t27 -- petal 8 (I ISSUES) of the interactive visualization epic.
; Refs epic t27#12173 (issue t27#12300). Built on specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27; the row it answers is
; row 8 of specs/t27f/petal_viz_plan.t27 (list + inspector + badge, truth VERIFIED).
; --
; Question: "Which open issue does the Queen pick next, and which label decided it?"
; Source of truth: specs/queen/priority.t27, the order the Queen should take open issues in. Every level,
; cap, aging step, blocker skip and reason below is a call into that file (capped_level, effective_level,
; eligible, outranks, why) and its label vocabulary (CRITICAL_LABELS .. LOW_LABELS); nothing of it is copied.
; --
; The one input the reader changes: a label chip. Each of the 7 fixture issues carries a subset of the four
; pool labels P0..P3; clicking (or activating by keyboard) a chip adds or removes that label on that issue and
; the list re-sorts. Remove P0 from the first issue and the fourth critical is no longer over the cap
; (CRITICAL_CAP), so a different issue is picked: the cap rule made visible.
; --
; Layers of this spec:
;   L1 state       PivState = the contract's one VizState + the label set (one bit per issue and label);
;                  piv_apply forwards every contract event to the one reducer viz_apply and adds ONE petal
;                  event, the label toggle.
;   L2 entities    issue i = viz_ref(NODE, i); the chip of label k on issue i = viz_ref(CELL, i * 4 + k).
;                  Focus order is the listing order (7 issues, then 28 chips), which does not change when
;                  the list re-sorts, so a focused item stays where it is.
;   L3 vocabulary  piv_label_level reads priority.t27's label strings (the source has the strings but no
;                  function from a label name to a level; `tri priority` does that step at runtime, and
;                  this petal does it the same way: the most urgent matching level wins).
;   L4 rules       piv_table runs the source functions over all 7 issues once: base level, criticals
;                  before, capped level, effective level, reason. Rank and pick are outranks/eligible.
;   L5 views       list (rows in priority order, with the label chips), inspector (one issue, label that
;                  decided it, reason), badge (the truth): all three read the ONE VizState.
;   L6 host        piv_host: badge, list and inspector as three root slots of a VizHost.
; --
; Truth. The fixture is a sample listing, and the rules over it are the source's own: the badge is
; VERIFIED while the labels are the fixture's. Changing a label leaves that data, so the badge becomes DEMO
; (what-if) and, through viz_may_claim, may not present the order as a result until the labels are the
; fixture's again. A reload keeps DEMO while the labels differ.
; --
; Integer only: no floats. Pixel geometry is in the list's own coordinates (origin = its top-left corner),
; so the hit test and the host agree without an offset.
; --
; Not claimed: no host draws this petal yet, and the fixture is not a live GitHub listing.

